       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 359-52
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7685726"
    >
Right-of-way of certain vehicles.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7685726" data-guid="7685726"></div>
        <div id="questions-7685726" data-guid="7685726" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7685726_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="history">[Amended <span class="legref" data-ref=""><span class="hisdate">8-7-1995</span> by <span class="loclaw">L.L. No. 6-1995</span></span>; <span class="legref" data-ref=""><span class="hisdate">5-20-1996</span> by <span class="loclaw">Ord. No. 9.51.96</span></span>]</div><div class="para">The employees of the Department of General Services, with their apparatus and vehicles of all kinds, when engaged in the work of cleaning the street or removing therefrom snow or refuse, and those persons with whom the City has contracted to perform such services, shall have the right-of-way in any street, and all other vehicles shall move in such a manner and to such positions as shall permit said apparatus and vehicle and the persons in charge thereof to clean the entire street.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
