<div class="section_content content" id="7685730_content" title-footnotes="1"><div class="footnotes"><div class="footnote" id="ft7685730-1"><a class="footnoterefnum" href="#ref7685730-1">[1]</a><div class="ftpara">Editor's Note: Former § 359-55, Lights, and § <a class="xref" guid="7685730" href="7685730#7685730">359-56</a>, Exceptions, were repealed 8-7-1995 by L.L. No. 6-1995.</div></div></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7685731"
      id="7685731"
      data-guid="7685731"
      data-position="8043"
      data-full-title="§ 359-57: Driving on sidewalks. "
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7685731_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7685731_label" for="7685731_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7685731"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 359-57
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7685731"
    >
Driving on sidewalks.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7685731" data-guid="7685731"></div>
        <div id="questions-7685731" data-guid="7685731" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7685731_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="history">[Amended <span class="legref" data-ref=""><span class="hisdate">8-7-1995</span> by <span class="loclaw">L.L. No. 6-1995</span></span>]</div><div class="para">No person shall drive a motor vehicle on or across a sidewalk, except that a vehicle may be driven at a reasonable speed, but not more than five miles per hour, on or across a sidewalk in such manner as not to interfere with the safety and passage of pedestrians thereon, who shall have the right-of-way, when it is reasonable and necessary:</div><div class="level"><div class="litem" id="7685732"><a alt="359-57A" class="litem_number" href="7685732#7685732" onclick="return false;" title="359-57A">A. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">To gain access to a public highway, private way or lands or buildings adjacent to such highway or way;</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="7685733"><a alt="359-57B" class="litem_number" href="7685733#7685733" onclick="return false;" title="359-57B">B. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">In the conduct of work upon a highway, or upon a private way or lands or buildings adjacent to such highway or way; or</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="7685734"><a alt="359-57C" class="litem_number" href="7685734#7685734" onclick="return false;" title="359-57C">C. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">To plow snow or perform any other public service, for hire, or otherwise, which could not otherwise be reasonably and properly performed.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div></div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7685735"
      id="7685735"
      data-guid="7685735"
      data-position="8047"
      data-full-title="§ 359-58: Emerging from alley, driveway, private road or building. "
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7685735_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7685735_label" for="7685735_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7685735"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 359-58
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7685735"
    >
Emerging from alley, driveway, private road or building.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7685735" data-guid="7685735"></div>
        <div id="questions-7685735" data-guid="7685735" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7685735_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="history">[Amended <span class="legref" data-ref=""><span class="hisdate">8-7-1995</span> by <span class="loclaw">L.L. No. 6-1995</span></span>]</div><div class="para">The driver of a vehicle emerging from an alley, driveway, private road or building shall stop such vehicle immediately prior to driving onto a sidewalk extending across any alleyway, building entrance, road or driveway or, in the event that there is no sidewalk, shall stop at the point nearest the roadway to be entered where the driver has a view of approaching traffic thereon.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7685736"
      id="7685736"
      data-guid="7685736"
      data-position="8048"
      data-full-title="§ 359-59: Construal."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
